1. She is half-Asian and has a strong connection to her English upbringing. (Verbatim: "I'm half, but even then, it's like, oh, but your brothers like spicy food, and even Papalia likes spicy food, where did you get this tongue from...")
2. She dislikes spicy foods and considers herself a "disappointing Asian" in her family. (Verbatim: "Mama Elia is very, very, very, very, very disappointed in that fact, actually, and has stated several times that I am a, quote, disappointing Asian...")
3. She is sensitive to the texture of nuts and finds them unpleasant in food. (Verbatim: "I don't like the texture of nuts okay I just don't um that's why I'm okay with like coconut based curries and almond based curries I like the flavors...")
4. She has a strong preference for non-spicy versions of Indian curries, especially tikka masala and korma. (Verbatim: "I do love a tikka masala, but it can't be spicy, a good tikka masala.")
5. She dislikes bone-in meat in curry and finds it upsetting. (Verbatim: "I get so upset if there's like bone in my curry it it upsets me um yeah and and like when i go to asialand and i have curry for my family sometimes there might be bone in it and i'll be like like why is there bone...")
6. She was unaware that beef could be tender and flavorful until she discovered it outside her family's cooking. (Verbatim: "I thought all beef tasted like that I thought all beef for the longest time was just this horrible chewy thing um and then i discovered that beef can actually be delicious...")
7. She grew up in England and did not have Indian takeaways during childhood due to her father's preference. (Verbatim: "We never had Indian takeaways because Papa Elia doesn't like, doesn't like Indian takeaways. So I didn't actually get to try Indian takeaways until, until I left, until, until I left with my family home.")
8. She enjoys hot chocolate but only has unusual flavors left, such as chili, orange, and mint. (Verbatim: "I've got like a gift set of hot chocolates. Okay. And I drank all the normal ones. So now the only ones left are like chili, orange, mint.")
9. She is fussy about the flavor and texture of korma, preferring it to have depth despite being non-spicy. (Verbatim: "I've realized a lot of them will just make them as like bland and forget that just because it has no spice doesn't mean it can't have any flavor...")
10. She is not fond of coconut or almonds despite enjoying their flavors in curries. (Verbatim: "I don't like coconut and I don't like almonds oh oh oh oh guess what guess what happened last night I had like the saddest dinner in the universe um okay so so so what happened was I I ordered a takeaway last night okay I ordered a takeaway last night and I thought I thought I'd go for something different um I went for a tie this time I went for a tie takeaway and I had a um what's it uh what's it called something um curry okay um and and and it arrived oh and I also got prawn crackers with it as well so I was like heck yeah prawn crackers um and and basically it arrived and first off I'd have the um ah masama and curry that's it masama and curry I had and um the the prawn crackers were too spicy for me the prawn crackers were spicy to begin with um so I was like ah rip and then the curry wasn't spicy the curry was actually delicious but but it had so many like physical nuts in it like so many nuts every every heck of bite every heck of bite was was it was a nut and I was like like why why why every bite was just nuts just nuts everywhere and I was like I don't want nuts now I just want I just want smooth curry I don't like nuts I don't like their texture that's it like I don't I don't I don't like the texture of nuts okay I just don't um that's why I'm okay with like coconut based curries and almond based curries I like the flavors the flavors okay but yeah I'll be honest I am weak I am I admit my weakness I am very weak um in fact oh gosh my stomach going um in fact um this is gonna make me sound even more weak um because I grew up so I grew up in England okay so you just you just gotta know that okay I grew up in England I grew up in England um we're talking about um food because I I love talking about food and you love talking about food we heckin love food yeah um so so when when mama like makes curry or if I go to Asia land and have curry um in England they're they they pretty much like exclusively use either well they exclusively use like chicken breast but if they're feeling really adventurous they'll use boneless chicken thigh um that is like the extent of english me okay we just don't we just don't you just don't use anything else we don't really use anything um but but i get so upset if there's like bone in my curry it it upsets me um yeah and and like when i go to asialand and i have curry for my family sometimes there might be bone in it and i'll be like like why is there bone beef is okay um oh don't tell don't tell mama elia i said this um the the the beef the beef that she cook would always be very very very very very very well done so it would be very very very very very chewy um and yeah i thought all beef tasted like that i thought all beef for the longest time was just this horrible chewy thing um and then i discovered i discovered that beef can actually be delicious and steak can actually be really nice it's just you gotta start making them super super i mean you know you know if you like it well that's fine that's fine that's fine um because my family love it well done but yeah yeah um i've realized beef is nice like yeah yeah i've actually it's just it was just mind-blowing how different a food can taste um like cook differently the same of like vegetables so like the traditional way to make english vegetables is to just boil it to an oblivion and it turns out if you like i don't know coat them in like honey and soy and roast them and it's just it could be delicious um it could be delicious as opposed to mushy um but mama elia does make some really delicious food she she is um she is very passionate about cooking so yes yes um yeah um we're here for q a i'm i'm just i'm just rambling um this was uh this was my hello how are you ramble um but yeah tangented a little bit just a just a little bit um let me put you guys there actually actually no let me um let me do this oh oh there we go i like this um so yes we're here for a q and a so it's a live q a because um youtube have a q a feature so that's how we're able to do it so i'm going to be using that um so please um ask me anything um i'm guessing usually if it's a q a after like a debut you can make it vtuber related um don't ask anything too spicy um okay because as you can tell by my mayonnaise is spicy um i'm not very spicy um yeah let me let me let me click") [end of text]



